🌒 Phase 2: Scheduled Silence Profiles

Right now you silence manually (1h / 4h / etc). Most noisy jobs have predictable times — e.g.:

during deploys

before ingestion completes

during ETL chain phases

during daily vendor pushes

So add:

Profile	Example
Daily window	“Silence every day 00:00–01:00”
Weekly window	“Mondays 06:00–08:00 (deploys)”
During business hours	“Mute alerts 09:00–17:00 Mon–Fri”
Cron-based	“Silence at 0 */3 * * * for 15m”
Environment-tied	“Mute during CI/CD rollout” (auto)
🔗 Phase 3: Follow-the-Parent Silence

Where job dependencies exist:

ETL → Indexing → Summary → API


If the ETL job is in maintenance for deploy, it makes no sense for indexing+summary to alert.

Feature:

“Silence this job when upstream X is silenced / late / deploying”

This keeps noise low and helps real SRE workflows.

🔧 Phase 4: Deployment-aware Silence

If you integrate with:

GitHub

GitLab

